# The public Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (qwen4exp) rows in one window: decode at depth 6 / 1024 / 3000 and
# prompt processing at P = 512 / 4096, bloomery (generate_qwen3moe on the qwen4exp UD-Q4_K_XL file,
# Body38, every routed expert on the host tier) against mainline llama.cpp (53ed051ce) at its best
# placement on the A6000: the profile's hand-set `-ngl 99 -fa on -lzm off -ncmoe 26 -t 32` and llama-bench's
# fit, each row publishing the faster (models/qwen4exp.sh). Runs only after proposal P8 gives
# tools/ref/depth-qwen3moe.sh its qwen4exp profile.
#
# The step is a sum, not a max: layer l+1 waits for layer l's combine, and only the shared expert
# overlaps the host's routed service. Per token, A6000, depth <= 2k [derived, q38prog stage A §4]:
#   card SMs     8.5..10 ms   (dense 4.83 GB at ~650 GB/s = 7.4 ms, + ~1.6 ms of latency floor
#                              over 1,151 nodes)
#   PCIe / sync  0.15..0.35   (the go and the wait of 48 layers, 3..7 us each; 20 KB a layer)
#   NVMe (PLE)   0.1..1.6     (16 IQ4_NL rows of 90 B a token, read serially in decode_input;
#                              0 when the table's pages are cached)
#   host DRAM    48 x h       (h: one layer's routed service, 18.4 MB gate-up + 12.3 MB down)
# h is the one term the derivation cannot fix: 390 us expected, 350..460 (the per-dispatch byte law,
# facts.md:108, at ~77 / ~62 GB/s for the two dispatches, +10..20 us fixed; ik's Qwen3.6 host tier
# 0.20 ms for 14.4 MB a layer, facts.md:64). So decode 30..38 tok/s at depth 6 and 1024, the same
# band at 3000 (the selected flash reads a fixed 2,051 rows: +12 x 2.1 MB).
# The prompt rows [derived]: --prefill step = decode, 30..37 tok/s at P = 512 and 4096; --prefill
# pass (passes of 8 through the batch port: the host union 74.8 distinct experts a layer, 23..32 us
# an expert, 82..115 ms over 48 layers, + card ~12 ms, eager enqueue and sync 2..5 ms) 60..80 tok/s
# at both P. llama.cpp's rows are the reference, not predicted here past "host-bound too"; its
# lcppfit / lcppppfit rows carry their fit column (a failed fit is a FAIL row, not a number).
kind: baseline
question: how long does one Qwen3.8 layer's routed service on the host tier take inside the
  decode step on the A6000, the one term the step derivation leaves open, and what are ours and
  llama.cpp's public Qwen3.8 rows in one window?
term: host service us a layer @ n=96, depth 6, A6000, all-host = (p50 step ms of the `6` arm of
  just depth-gpu-qwen4exp - 8.5..10 ms card - 0.25..1.95 ms sync and PLE) / 48, the card and sync
  terms at their band centres (9.25 and 1.1 ms)
unit: us
predict: 350..460
condition: one lease, three rounds, arms 6 lcpp:6 512 lcpppp:512 1024 lcpp:1024 3000 lcpp:3000 4096
  lcpppp:4096 lcpppp4096:4096 lcppfit:6 lcppppfit4096:4096 in engine blocks (BLOOMERY_AB_ORDER=blocks:
  ours, lcpp and lcppfit blocks, each opened by a discarded process that pages that engine's host set
  in); each ours arm's row carries its prompt's pass pp, so the 512 and 4096 arms give pp512 and
  pp4096; about 65 minutes of lease [derived: five ours arms of a 20..80 s load, up to 56 s of passes
  and 3 s of steps, seven llama.cpp arms of a host-bound load and run, three rounds, and ~5 minutes
  for the three discards], past 30: the user's approval first; every row carries its majflt field,
  and no row tagged [cold] (major faults at 75 us each over 1 % of its timed window) is admitted;
  no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]; the full runner output goes to a file first. Command:
  BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38-public.card
  BLOOMERY_AB_ORDER=blocks' just depth-gpu-qwen4exp <the arms above> > <log> 2>&1
reason: sets the public Qwen3.8 rows (decode and prompt processing, llama.cpp beside ours) and
  the host service term every later Qwen3.8 lever is priced against (hot list, card experts, the
  q38ub ubatch round); why now: the final sitting takes every model's table in one window, and
  Qwen3.8 has no timed number yet
decide-in: write the rows into rig-log first, then the README's Qwen3.8 section, ratios from this
  window only; each llama.cpp row publishes the faster of its hand-set and fit arms; the README's
  table carries decode, and llama.cpp's pp beside it; our pp rows (8-position passes, kind=pass) go
  to rig-log only, marked the pass path's — the baseline q38ub is judged against, as GLM's are
decide-below: the host tier serves faster than the byte law says for 3 MB experts: name the term
  (the dispatch rate or the fixed cost) against V4.1's measured union, re-derive the card-expert
  and hot-list levers from the lower h before any lever round opens, then write the rows
decide-above: no Qwen3.8 row goes out: nsys-gpu.sh has no qwen4exp form, so a round gives it one,
  profiles one depth-6 step to split h into the gate-up and down dispatches and the go/wait gaps,
  and names the term that missed (dispatch rate, a serial host cost such as the PLE read, or the
  union's fixed term) before a re-sit
